preConditionHook:
// ARM THE BREAKEVEN STOP STRUCTURALLY, NOT ON A DOLLAR AMOUNT. The stop to
// breakeven is armed only after the trade has held on its own side of the
// exponential average for barsAboveEma CONSECUTIVE bars SINCE ENTRY; once armed,
// a close back at the entry price takes the trade off.
//
// Kept apart from BreakevenStop, whose trigger is peak profit reaching a dollar
// figure: a four-bar rally holding above the average and a $100 peak arm on
// completely different bars, and neither is a parameter setting of the other.
//
// THE COUNTER AND THE ARMED FLAG ARE PER POSITION and are reset on
// BarsSinceEntry() == 0 -- VERIFIED as 0 on the fill bar and as restarting
// through a reversal, so the count really is "since entry" even when the
// position was opened by a reversal, which a MarketPosition() == 0 reset would
// miss. While flat the reset simply repeats. The counter advances on the fill
// bar too, so a fill bar closing above the average is the first of the run.
//
// MultiWalk's WFSafe_Xaverage, which the EasyLanguage twin calls. MEASURED
// (EL_XAverage_Probe.txt, @OJ 240min) bit-identical to the plain XAverage
// built-in AT A FIXED LENGTH -- (wf - xa) exactly 0 on all 17,785 bars. SEED is
// the PRICE on the study's first calculated bar (ctx.CurrentBar() == 1), not a
// length-term simple average; the recurrence is ONE statement in EL's own form,
// x + sf*(p - x), never sf*p + (1-sf)*x, which separates on 67% of bars past
// 100. NO WARM-UP HOLE: do not add a CurrentBar() < n guard returning 0. An EMA
// never forgets its seed, so the seed bar is part of the specification and moves
// with Max Bars Back and the chart start. The walkforward LENGTH CHANGE is
// UNMEASURED, so emaLength MUST BE PINNED in the grid. Only the current value is
// read; the lagged read is unmeasured and not needed here.
emaSf = 2.0 / (emaLength + 1.0);
if (ctx.CurrentBar() == 1) {
    emaVal = close[0];
} else {
    emaVal = emaVal + emaSf * (close[0] - emaVal);
}
if (ctx.BarsSinceEntry() == 0) {
    barsAboveCnt = 0;
    barsBelowCnt = 0;
    armedLong = false;
    armedShort = false;
}
if (el_gt(close[0], emaVal)) {
    barsAboveCnt = barsAboveCnt + 1;
} else {
    barsAboveCnt = 0;
}
if (el_lt(close[0], emaVal)) {
    barsBelowCnt = barsBelowCnt + 1;
} else {
    barsBelowCnt = 0;
}
if (el_ge((double)barsAboveCnt, barsAboveEma)) armedLong = true;
if (el_ge((double)barsBelowCnt, barsAboveEma)) armedShort = true;
